r <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b24-cln_65p548">24</xref>: &#x0201c;Mean 24-hour profile of plasma TSH during a 53-hour period including 8 hours of nocturnal sleep (black bar), 28 hours of continuous wakefulness (nocturnal hours: white bar), and 8 hours of daytime sleep (black bar at the right). Subjects were young healthy men. The shadow area corresponds to normal 24-hour conditions. The vertical bar at each time point represents the standard error of the mean (SEM) ...&#x0201d; (Pannain S, Van Cauter E. Sleep Medicine Clinics 2007; 2: 147&#x02013;159).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="cln_65p548f2"/></fig><fig id="f3-cln_65p548" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>A diagram showing the effects of CYP450 inducers or inhibitors on TH metabolism and the final results of these pharmacological actions on T4 and T3 levels. Thyroid hormones (THs); Thyroxine (T4); Triiodo-thyronine (T3).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="cln_65p548f3"/></fig></floats-group></article>